ss does not claim artifacts that are intentionally out of scope. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-02 | The root and goal progress trackers still contain `<short description>` placeholders for the goal and every step. These are handoff/process artifacts, and the placeholders prevent a future executor or reviewer from using the trackers as a durable summary of scope and status. | Replace each placeholder in `progress.md` and `01-button-chain-html/progress.md` with the concrete goal/step descriptions from the inventory, while keeping all implementation statuses incomplete for the planning-only proof. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-03 | `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` compresses the full browser proof into one row with a generic target of \"Current last visible button.\" That is too broad for the direct-interaction cache required by the UI validation reference and weakens proof of the exact sequence: initial button creates generated 1, generated 1 creates generated 2, generated 2 creates generated 3, generated 3 creates generated 4, generated 4 clears the document. | Split the run cache into ordered direct-input rows with distinct targets/readiness checks for each click and expected count/result after each click, including the terminal assertion that only bordered `finished` remains. | ❌ unresolved |\n\n## Verdict\n\n- Status: `💤 pending`\n- Rationale: unresolved process and UI-proof artifacts remain. Do not approve the plan until AR-01 through AR-03 are addressed and the review is rerun.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
